; BOUNCE BONANZA - song 2, course 2: "Bounce Trial" (SPEC.md 128.20)
;
; D dorian at 136.5 BPM - a 16th is one row of SIX sub-ticks (110 ms),
; straight 16ths, two 4/4 bars a pattern (3.5 s).
;
; The rubber ball's course, so the tune BOUNCES: its motif is an octave
; spring - a low note, the same note an octave up a 16th later, then a
; syncopated fall through the chord that lands a 16th before the beat.
; Funk in D dorian: the Dm7 - G7 vamp (the dorian's major IV), a slap bass
; that pops octaves on the off 16ths, and chord stabs on the "and"s.
;
; Intro: the slap bass alone (the speaker plays it: `spkbass`), the stabs
; join, and the lead springs down a G7 scale onto the motif.
; A  (4 patterns): the motif over Dm7 - G7, twice; a higher answer; then the
;    funk turnaround Bb - C - Dm7 (the borrowed bVI - bVII - i).
; B  (4 patterns): contrast - Fmaj7 G7 | Em7 Am7 | again | A7sus4 A7, long
;    ARPEGGIATED notes (chiparp / chiparpm sparkle on both arms), disco
;    octave bass, straight off-beat stabs, claps instead of snares.
; C  (2 patterns): the BREAK - the lead only answers the bass with short
;    octave bounces, then the bass drops out and the ball is pumped up:
;    ten bounces, each higher and sooner than the last, under a snare roll,
;    the last one (C6, the dorian's flat seventh) falling onto the loop's D.
; Intro, A A A A, B B B B, C C - 35 s a loop.
;
; On the speaker the LEAD carries it (q0: no gaps, so the bass is heard
; only in the lead's written rests - the octave pops between the motif's
; notes); kick, snare and clap blip on the beats, hats are chip-only.

song trial "Bounce Trial"
groove 6
unit 16
rows 32
measure 16
spkbass
voice lead chip
voice bass pluckbass
voice chord stab

; A note followed by a written rest is spelled as ONE note with a `q` gap
; (`q6 d8` = d16 r16): the same sound on both arms, two bytes fewer.

; --- the intro: slap bass alone, then the lead springs down onto the motif ---
lead LI  = q0 r:18 o4 q6 d8 >d8 <d8 q0 >d8 c16 <b16 a16 g16 f16 e16 |

; --- A: the motif (Dm7 | G7) ------------------------------------------------------
lead LA1 = q0 o4 d8 q6 >d8 q0 c8 <a16 >c8. <a8 g16 q12 a8. |
           q0 g8 q6 >g8 q0 f8 d16 f8. d8 c16 q12 <b8. |
lead LA2 = q0 o4 d8 q6 >d8 q0 c8 <a16 >c8. <a8 g16 q12 a8. |
           q0 g8 a16 b16 >c16 q6 d8 q0 e16 f8 e16 q6 d8 q0 c16 <b8 |
lead LA3 = q0 o4 a8 q6 >a8 q0 g8 f16 a8. f8 e16 q12 d8. |
           q0 d8 <b16 q6 >d8 q0 d16 c16 <b16 a8 g8 f8 e8 |
lead LA4 = q0 o4 f8 a16 q6 >d8 q0 c16 <a8 g8 >c16 q6 e8 q0 d16 c8 |
           q6 d:7 q0 c16 d8 <a8 >d8 e8 |
bass BA  = o2 d8. >d16 <d8 d16 >d8 c16 <a8 >c16 d8 <a16 |
           g8. >g16 <g8 g16 >g8 f16 d8 f16 g8 d16 |
bass BA4 = o2 b-8. >b-16 <b-8 >b-8 c8. >c16 <c8 >c8 |
           o2 d8. >d16 <d8 >d16 c16 <a8 >c8 <d8 e8 |
; the stabs: each a long event whose gate (q) is cut to about 8 sub-ticks
chord CA = o4 v10 r8 q16 [f a >c]4 q10 [f a >c]:3 q4 [f a >c]8 q34 [f a >c]:7
           q16 [f b >d]4 q10 [f b >d]:3 q4 [f b >d]8 q22 [f b >d]:5
chord CA4 = o4 v10 q10 [f b- >d]8. [f b- >d]8. q4 [f b- >d]8 q10 [g >c e]8. [g >c e]8. q4 [g >c e]8 |
            q28 [f a >c]4. q52 [f a >c]:10 |
drum DA  = k4 s8. k8. k8 s4 | k4 s4 k16 k8. s8 c8 |
drum DF  = k4 s8. k8. k8 s4 | k4 s8 k8 T16 T16 t16 t16 s16 s16 s8 |

; --- B: Fmaj7 G7 | Em7 Am7 | Fmaj7 G7 | A7sus4 A7 - held, arpeggiated --------------
lead LB1 = q0 o5 f8 e16 @chiparpm a16^4^8 @chip g8 e8 c8 | d8 e16 @chiparp g16^4^8 @chip f8 e8 d8 |
lead LB2 = q0 o5 @chiparp g4 @chip e8 d8 @chiparpm e4 @chip g8 b8 | @chiparpm a4. @chip g16 e16 c8 d8 e8 g8 |
lead LB4 = q0 o5 d8 e16 q6 g8 q0 e16 d8 @chiparpm q12 e:8 |
           q0 @chiparp a8 @chip >c+16 q6 <a8 g8 q0 e16 c+8 q12 <a4 q0 >c+8 |
bass BB1 = o2 f4. >f8 <f8 >f8 <f4 | g4. >g8 <g8 >g8 f8 e8 |
bass BB2 = o2 e4. >e8 <e8 >e8 <e4 | a4. >a8 <a8 >a8 <g8 e8 |
bass BB4 = o2 a4. >a8 <a8 >a8 <a4 | a4. >a8 g8 e8 c+8 <a8 |
chord CB1 = o4 v10 q16 r8 [e a >c]4 [e a >c]4 [e a >c]4 [e a >c]4 [d g b]4 [d g b]4 [d g b]4 q4 [d g b]8
chord CB2 = o4 v10 q16 r8 [d g b]4 [d g b]4 [d g b]4 [d g b]4 [e a >c]4 [e a >c]4 [e a >c]4 q4 [e a >c]8
chord CB4 = o4 v10 q16 r8 [d e a]4 [d e a]4 [d e a]4 [d e a]4 [c+ e g]4 [c+ e g]4 [c+ e g]4 q4 [c+ e g]8
drum DB  = k4 c4 k8 k8 c4 | k4 c4 k8. k16 c8 c8 |

; --- C: the break - bounces answering the bass, then the ball pumped up ------------
lead LC1 = q0 r2 o5 q6 d8 <d8 >c8 q0 <a8 | r2 q6 g8 >g8 f8 q0 d8 |
lead LC2 = o4 q30 d:6 q24 f:5 g:5 | q18 a:4 q12 >c:3 d:3 q6 f:2 g:2 q0 a16 >c16 |
chord CC2 = o4 v10 q4 [f a >c]8 r:30

order LI  BA  CA  DF          ; 0: the intro
order LA1 BA  CA  DA          ; 1: the loop comes back here
order LA2 BA  CA  DA
order LA3 BA  CA  DA
order LA4 BA4 CA4 DF
order LB1 BB1 CB1 DB
order LB2 BB2 CB2 DB
order LB1 BB1 CB1 DB
order LB4 BB4 CB4 DF
order LC1 BA  CA  DB
order LC2 -   CC2 DF 
loop 1
